      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Pleasanton Railroad Depot, built in 1890, still stands at the town’s center, a relic of the era’s rail boom.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pleasanton%2C_Nebraska",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Pleasanton’s first schoolhouse, built on the south side of the South Loup River, served students until a 1909 brick building replaced it.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
